🔥 Project 1: CI/CD Pipeline using Jenkins, Docker & AWS
🎯 Project Goal
Automatically deploy an application when code is pushed to GitHub.
Copy code

GitHub → Jenkins → Docker Build → Deploy on AWS EC2
Also:
Container should restart automatically
Application should come back after server reboot

🧱 Tech Stack
GitHub
Jenkins
Docker
AWS EC2 (Ubuntu)
Django Todo Application
🧩 Architecture Flow
Copy code

Developer pushes code to GitHub
        ↓
      Jenkins pulls code
        ↓
     Docker image build
        ↓
   Docker container runs
        ↓
      AWS EC2

✅ Step 1: AWS EC2 Setup
OS: Ubuntu 20.04
Instance type: t2.micro
Open ports:
22 (SSH)
8080 (Jenkins)
8000 (Application)

✅ Step 2: Jenkins Installation
Installed OpenJDK 21
Installed and configured Jenkins
Jenkins runs on port 8080

✅ Step 3: Docker Installation
Installed Docker on EC2
Added Jenkins user to Docker group
Restarted Jenkins to apply permissions

✅ Step 4: GitHub Integration
Generated GitHub Personal Access Token
Added token to Jenkins credentials
Configured Jenkins to pull code securely

✅ Step 5: Dockerfile
Dockerfile
Copy code
FROM python:3.9
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
RUN pip install --upgrade pip
RUN pip install django==3.2
CMD ["python", "manage.py", "runserver", "0.0.0.0:8000"]

✅ Step 6: Jenkins Job Configuration
Created Jenkins Freestyle Job
Connected GitHub repository
Added shell build step:
Bash
Copy code
docker build -t todo-app .
docker stop todo || true
docker rm todo || true
docker run -d \
--name todo \
--restart=always \
-p 8000:8000 \
todo-app

✅ Step 7: Testing
Pushed code to GitHub
Jenkins triggered automatically
Application accessible at:
Copy code

http://<EC2-IP>:8000
After server reboot, container starts automatically
📌 Key Learnings
Jenkins CI/CD pipeline creation
GitHub authentication using tokens
Docker image build and deployment
Handling build failures and debugging
Container auto-restart using Docker restart policies

AWS EC2 deployment

🎤 One-line Interview Explanation
“I built a CI/CD pipeline where Jenkins pulls code from GitHub, builds a Docker image, and deploys a Django application on AWS EC2 with automatic container restart.”